Changes in v3:
  - the mailbox receive callback only queues work; rproc_vq_interrupt()
    runs from an ordered workqueue
  - teardown: rproc_del(), then the mailbox channel is freed, then the
    work is cancelled
  - cfg, remap and both SRAM regions are required
  - address translation covers only the two SRAM windows; DRAM, trace
    and vrings come from the carveouts (Sashiko)
  - crash interrupt armed and disarmed with an atomic bit (Sashiko)
  - kick payloads are static per-vring constants (Sashiko)
  - boot address and remap writes are read back before the reset is
    released (Sashiko)
  - runtime PM powers the RISC-V and SRAM domains; debug reset handled
  - one mailbox channel instead of two
  - A733 (sun60i) support dropped
